                                "sense_id": "9a624adb-50a9-3b39-9b24-586f66cba99d",
                                "text": "I druther stay home today."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "afa4cd2e-b371-4ce3-ad01-a9d6433ede10",
                                "sense_id": "9a624adb-50a9-3b39-9b24-586f66cba99d",
                                "text": "We druther go swimming than go to school."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "98bcd2fd-324e-4538-87fa-f032f6ac4ef3",
                                "sense_id": "9a624adb-50a9-3b39-9b24-586f66cba99d",
                                "text": "The old gentleman was for going along with me, but I said no, I could drive the horse myself, and I druther he wouldn't take no trouble about me."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "747d0b60-ccb5-4e47-bed0-de4dfb517cb9",
                                "sense_id": "9a624adb-50a9-3b39-9b24-586f66cba99d",
                                "text": "\"He's no slouch at dog-breakin', that's wot I say,\" one of the men on the wall cried enthusiastically. / \"Druther break cayuses any day, and twice on Sundays,\" was the reply of the driver, as he climbed on the wagon and started the horses."
                            }
